<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#portuguese-language">Glossary</a> · Term · language</p><h1 class="enc-title">Portuguese language</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Portuguese is a Romance language that originated in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a>. Spread by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>, it is now spoken by over 250 million people in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a> and other countries. It was also used in the administration of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo Empire</a> after its rulers adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/portuguese-language.jpg" alt="Portuguese language" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Victorcouto · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Breve_discurso_em_que_se_contem_a_conquista_do_Reyno_de_Pegu_na_%C3%8Dndia_Oriental,_pelos_portuguezes_em_tempo_do_Viso-Rey_Ayres_de_Saldanha;_sendo_capitam_Salvador_Ribeiro_de_Souza,_chamado_Massinga,_natural_de_Guimaraens._Rei_do_Pegu.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
